package software edition "2026-11-12"

namespace software:
    primitive text, person

    section "Programs":

        A program means a text that a computer runs.
        A command means a program that a person runs by name.
        A subcommand means a command that is a part of a command.
        An option means a word of a command line that changes the behavior of a command.
        An exit status means the number that a command returns.
        An editor means a program that shows a text to a person.
        A language server means a program that serves an editor.

    section "Files":

        A file means a named text that a computer keeps.
        A directory means a named set of files.
        A path means the name that locates a file or a directory.
        A digest means the SHA-256 value of a file.
